Task 1 (#972, the DREAM milestone path): Make record_green_validation_to (the function that writes green-run validation rows) also record whether each surprise file existed yet at the snapshot's commit. That check only needs the snapshot's commit hash and the file paths, and both are available there.
• Since Sept 22 this function has written 15 rows with none of the readings. The assessment traced the gap to it, not to /risk validate as #972 says. It labels its rows trigger: "cli", which is how the issue got pointed at the wrong code.
• I'm taking a third risk-subsystem task despite the trajectory's concentration warning, on purpose: it's a filed issue, it was already put off once for this same reason, and it's the dream's next step. The other slot goes to a different subsystem.
• The tests must run the real writer and read the row back with the real parser: one file created after the snapshot, one that already existed, and one commit hash that doesn't resolve. That last one must read "unmeasured", never 0. The positive control breaks and restores the fix in a single command.
• If the function turns out to record this already, the task makes no code change and reports why those 15 rows lack it.

Task 2 (#936, first slice, a product fix): Some REPL-only commands typed at the shell with extra words (e.g. yoyo checkpoint save) start a paid model turn instead of being refused. This slice covers only the commands whose valid second words are already defined in the source as a subcommand list.
• A command is refused only when its second word is in that list, so ordinary sentences like yoyo plan the migration still reach the model.
• Commands where the pair could plausibly start a real prompt are left out, each with a comment naming why.
• There are tests confirming such sentences still get through, and a positive control.

